This is my second ascension (first one was in august with a
wizard) and first one on NAO. The full dumpfile is available at:
http://alt.org/nethack/dumplog/chlorine.lastgame.txt

A huge thanks to the people on #nethack who helped me
while I was on the planes! :)

I had started to play rangers and become good with them
shortly after my ascension. Throwing daggers is awesome,
and I like gnomish rangers because they start with a cloak
of displacement.
There was nothing particularly eventful about this game
I guess. Sokoban gave me a bag of holding, I found a bone
files of a wizard which gave me a cursed cloak of magic
resistance, but I did not use it until much later in the game
because I had a gray dragon scale mail at the time. I found
an amulet of reflection (identified it by zapping wands on
walls and having ther ray bounce on me).
I spent most of the game with gray dragon scale mail +
amulet of reflection + robe, until I found silver scales in
vlad tower, where I changed to silver dragon scale mail
+ cloak of magic resistance + amulet of life saving (I had
5 or 6 of those when I entered astral plane).

First (and only) sacrifice gift was Magicbane. I also
got Vorpal Blade when I got crowned. I used Vorpal Blade
for most of the game, and switched to Magicbane for
the curse absorbtion before going to wake Rodney.

One mistake I made was to quaff a potion of gain level
when I was only at level 12. I didn't find another one, so
I had to go all the way down to the castle to reach level
14 by killing monsters.

I kiled a cockatrice in Moloch's sanctum, and used it
corpse to turn everything around me (except wraithes)
to stone. This was the first time I wielded a cockatrice
corpse and this was fun. I guess Moloch's sanctum is
so crowded it must be one of the nicest place to do that.

Planes of earth, fire and water were easy (fire with some
annoying salamanders but no sweat). I spent some time
blind on air, before realizing that there were an abnormally
large number of "invisible" air elementals.
I could kill easily one air elemental while it was swallowing
me, so I killed a couple that way, rested in steam or energy
vortices, and teleported the others away.

Astral plane was messy, but I guess it always is.
The rider that frightened me the most was death and he
was on the right. So I headed to the middle, guarded by
pestilence. I teleported monsters away with wands of
teleport (I had quite a number of them thanks to advice
on #nethack) and dealed with pestilence (and later
famine) with wands of death. The middle altar was cahotic,
so I made my way out of the temple and went left.
I died once to Famine there but had lots of amulets of
life saving.
I put a ring of conflict on, and it was a great help. Famine
was still attacking me though so I zapped him with a wand
of death and it worked the first time.
I went easily inside the temple because nobody was paying
much attention to me, and it was the right temple.

